<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">Alert</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    A modal dialog for displaying important messages that require user acknowledgement before continuing.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <Button modal="alert-info">Show Alert</Button>
    <Alert id="alert-info" title="Heads up!" description="This is an informational alert." variant="info"/>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<Button modal=\"my-alert\">Show</Button>\n<Alert id=\"my-alert\" title=\"Title\" description=\"Description\" variant=\"info\"/>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      An Alert is a two-part pattern: a trigger element with a <code>modal</code> prop pointing to the
      alert's <code>id</code>, and the Alert component itself. The alert renders as a fixed overlay
      and is hidden until the trigger is clicked.
    </p>
  </Prose>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-muted/50 overflow-hidden mt-4">
    <CodeBlock code={"Button (modal=\"my-alert\")\n└── opens ─→ Alert (id=\"my-alert\")\n                ├── Icon (based on variant)\n                ├── Title\n                ├── Description\n                └── Action Button"}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Alerts are for messages that demand attention and a conscious response. They interrupt the
      current workflow on purpose — the user must acknowledge the message before they can continue
      interacting with the page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use alerts for success confirmations, warnings about irreversible actions, error notifications,
      or informational messages that the user should not miss. If the message is purely informational
      and does not need acknowledgement, consider an inline banner or toast notification instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      For actions that need a choice (confirm / cancel), use a
      <a href="/components/confirmation-dialog">Confirmation Dialog</a> instead.
      For complex forms or multi-step workflows, use a
      <a href="/components/dialog">Dialog</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      When opened, the alert displays a backdrop overlay that dims the rest of the page. The page
      scroll is locked and focus is trapped inside the alert panel.
    </p>
    <p>
      By default, alerts are <strong>dismissible</strong> — the user can close them by clicking the
      close button, pressing Escape, or clicking the backdrop. Set <code>dismissible={false}</code> to
      create a strict alert that can only be dismissed by clicking the action button. This is useful for
      legal acceptances, mandatory acknowledgements, or critical error states.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each variant automatically displays an appropriate icon: a checkmark for success, a triangle for
      warnings, an exclamation circle for danger, and an info circle for informational alerts. The
      default variant shows no icon.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Variants -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Success</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Confirms a completed action. Shows a checkmark icon.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Button modal="alert-success">Show Alert</Button>
      <Alert id="alert-success" title="Success" description="Operation completed successfully." variant="success"/>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Warning</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Warns about a potentially risky action. Shows a triangle exclamation icon.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Button modal="alert-warning">Show Alert</Button>
      <Alert id="alert-warning" title="Warning" description="Please proceed with caution." variant="warning"/>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Danger</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Indicates an error or destructive outcome. Shows a circle exclamation icon.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Button modal="alert-danger">Show Alert</Button>
      <Alert id="alert-danger" title="Danger" description="Something went wrong." variant="danger"/>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Non-dismissible</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>
        No close button, no backdrop dismiss, no Escape key. The user <strong>must</strong> click the
        action button to continue. Use sparingly — only when the acknowledgement is genuinely required.
      </p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Button modal="alert-nodismiss">Show Alert</Button>
      <Alert id="alert-nodismiss" title="Terms Updated" description="Please review and accept the updated terms of service to continue." variant="warning" dismissible={false} button_text="I Accept"/>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Custom Button Text</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>
        Override the default "OK" label with something more specific to the context. Action-oriented
        labels like "Install Now" or "I Accept" help the user understand what will happen.
      </p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <Button modal="alert-custom">Show Alert</Button>
      <Alert id="alert-custom" title="Update Available" description="A new version is ready to install." variant="info" button_text="Install Now"/>
    '}/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Keep the title short and the description actionable.</li>
          <li>Match the variant to the severity of the message.</li>
          <li>Use specific button labels that describe the action ("I Accept", "Got it").</li>
          <li>Reserve non-dismissible alerts for legally or functionally mandatory acknowledgements.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use alerts for routine feedback that doesn't need interruption.</li>
          <li>Stack multiple alerts on the same trigger — show one at a time.</li>
          <li>Make every alert non-dismissible; users will learn to resent them.</li>
          <li>Put complex forms or long content inside an alert — use a Dialog instead.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">id</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any unique ID</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">title</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any text</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">description</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any text</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">variant</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Symbol</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">default, success, warning, danger, info</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">default</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">dismissible</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">size</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Symbol</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">sm, default, lg, xl, full</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">default</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">button_text</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any text</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">"OK"</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
